      "text": "God alone knows men’s thoughts, D&C 6:16 (33:1). look unto God in every thought, D&C 6:36. you took no thought save it was to ask, D&C 9:7. if it is not right, you shall have stupor of thought, D&C 9:9. the Lord is discerner of thoughts, D&C 33:1. let morrow take thought for things of itself, D&C 84:81, 84. cast away idle thoughts, D&C 88:69. secret thoughts to be revealed, D&C 88:109. speak thoughts that the Lord shall put into hearts, D&C 100:5. let virtue garnish thy thoughts, D&C 121:45.",
